Say which step of the matching did not come back

The photograph of run 545 says where the boot stopped, and it says it
twice over: the last mark on the panel is the result of AppleARMPU's
probe, and the mark that should follow it -- the one that says the
candidate was taken into the start list -- is not there.  So the run
stopped between the two, and there are four things in between:

  inst->detach (this);                      the instance leaves the provider
  newInst->setProperty (gIOProbeScoreKey);  the score is written down
  startList->setObject (newInst);           the instance goes on the list
  props->release ();                        the properties are let go

The first of them takes the I/O lock, and the matching already holds
it, so it is the one to look at.  But a picture says which and not why,
so each step now leaves a mark of its own: D1 after the probe returned,
D2 after the detach, D3 after the score was written, D4 after the
instance went on the list, D5 after the properties were let go and D6
after the instance was.  The last D on the panel is the step that did
not come back.

And the personalities are started after the candidates are gathered, so
that phase gets two marks as well: S1 before a personality is started
and S2 after it came back.  A personality's start() is a place where a
board's own driver can stop, and the storage driver's start() is the
one this port has watched for a long time.

Every mark goes to the panel the way the matching's other marks go,
through the console blob's own writer, so that it appears even when the
console path is the thing that is stuck.

